/-!
# Local control reductions for E.4.2

The invariant space inside each local two-core is fixed by all earlier
corank-family members in that overgroup. Kernel and Sylow-normalizer
generation consequently preserves every later weak fixed space. A maximal
subfamily argument proves the desired bound conditional on this local
invariance, or on relative normality of the kernel times the Sylow subgroup.

The prime-order local quotient case discharges that condition from the
genuine source hypotheses. The quasisimple case remains to be proved.
No unconditional E.4.2 theorem, or counterexample to its full local
residual-control assertion, is claimed here. The source theorem's final
assembly belongs to GenerationBound.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004, E.4.2,
printed p.241 (PDF p.252).
-/
